  "conclusion": "EXP-08 isolates the effect of BoT-SORT motion association and Camera Motion Compensation (GMC) strictly without appearance ReID. The results demonstrate that camera motion compensation (sparse optical flow) is the decisive driver of player association quality on broadcast football, improving Macro AssA by +0.0354 and IDF1 by +0.0296 across 6 sequences (4500 frames), while cutting ID switches by 21.1%. Throughput remains well above broadcast real-time at 39.5 FPS."
